4. MODIFY the StandardCard component:
      - Update props: StandardCard({ standard, strand, subStrand }) — add strand and subStrand props.
      - Add local state: const [drawer, setDrawer] = useState({ open: false, title: '', content: '', loading: false, error: null }).
      - When the card is expanded (open === true) and indicatorCount > 0, render each indicator li with 4 action buttons appended after the indicator code+description:
          <div className="flex flex-wrap gap-1 mt-2">
            <button onClick={() => handleAI('lesson', ind)} className="text-xs rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent px-2 py-0.5 hover:bg-accent/20">✨ Generate Lesson</button>
            <button onClick={() => handleAI('activities', ind)} className="text-xs rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent px-2 py-0.5 hover:bg-accent/20">📋 Generate Activities</button>
            <button onClick={() => handleAI('assessment', ind)} className="text-xs rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent px-2 py-0.5 hover:bg-accent/20">📝 Generate Assessment</button>
            <button onClick={() => handleAI('explain', ind)} className="text-xs rounded-full bg-accent/10 text-accent px-2 py-0.5 hover:bg-accent/20">💡 Explain</button>
          </div>
      - Implement handleAI(type, indicator):
          const context = { strand, subStrand, contentStandard: standard, indicators: [indicator] };
          setDrawer({ open: true, title: titleMap[type], content: '', loading: true, error: null });
          try {
            let result;
            if (type === 'lesson') {
              const plan = await generateLessonPlan(context);
              result = formatLessonPlan(plan); // see below
            } else if (type === 'activities') {
              result = await generateActivities(context);
            } else if (type === 'assessment') {
              result = await generateAssessment(context);
            } else {
              result = await explainIndicator({ indicator, ...context });
            }
            setDrawer(d => ({ ...d, loading: false, content: result }));
          } catch (e) {
            setDrawer(d => ({ ...d, loading: false, error: e.message }));
          }
      - formatLessonPlan(plan): converts the JSON plan object to a readable multi-section string:
          `STARTER ACTIVITY\n${plan.starterActivity}\n\nMAIN LEARNING\n${plan.mainLearning}\n\nPLENARY\n${plan.plenary}\n\nKEY QUESTIONS\n${plan.keyQuestions}\n\nRESOURCES SUGGESTED\n${plan.resourcesSuggested}\n\nHOMEWORK\n${plan.homework}`
      - After a successful 'lesson' generation, append a 'Plan this in Planner →' button in the drawer footer area (inside the AIDrawer, only visible when type==='lesson' and !loading and content). On click, call navigate('/planner') (import useNavigate from react-router-dom in Curriculum.jsx).
      - Render <AIDrawer open={drawer.open} onClose={() => setDrawer(d=>({...d,open:false}))} title={drawer.title} content={drawer.content} loading={drawer.loading} error={drawer.error} /> at the bottom of the StandardCard return, outside the card div (portalled into body isn't needed since the drawer is fixed).

   e. Update the strand rendering loop in the main Curriculum component to pass strand and subStrand down:
      <StandardCard key={std.id} standard={std} strand={activeStrand} subStrand={ss} />
